/T (The front end is a single-page application \(SPA\) written in React 19. In a single-page application the browser loads one HTML document \(index.html\) and a JavaScript bundle once; afterwards, React renders and replaces screens in the browser without full page reloads. This gives the portal the responsiveness of a desktop application: moving from the Residents page to the Payments page happens instantly, and the shared sidebar and navigation bar remain on screen.)
/E (The front end is a single-page application \(SPA\) written in React 19. In a single-page application the browser loads one HTML document \(index.html\) and a JavaScript bundle once; afterwards, React renders and replaces screens in the browser without full page reloads. This gives the portal the responsiveness of a desktop application: moving from the Residents page to the Payments page happens instantly, and the shared sidebar and navigation bar remain on screen.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
