/T (MySQL 8 was chosen as the database because society data is naturally relational. Flats have residents; flats receive bills; bills receive payments made by residents; residents raise complaints and book amenities. These relationships are best represented with tables, primary keys, and foreign keys, and they benefit from the integrity guarantees of a relational database management system.)
