/T (The back end is the layer that will receive requests from the React application, apply business rules and security checks, and read from or write to the MySQL database. In the current release, the back end is represented by the service layer \(src/services/api.js\), which exposes asynchronous list, add, update, and remove functions for every resource and simulates network latency of 180 milliseconds. This allowed the complete user interface to be built and tested before the server was written.)
/E (The back end is the layer that will receive requests from the React application, apply business rules and security checks, and read from or write to the MySQL database. In the current release, the back end is represented by the service layer \(src/services/api.js\), which exposes asynchronous list, add, update, and remove functions for every resource and simulates network latency of 180 milliseconds. This allowed the complete user interface to be built and tested before the server was written.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
