/T (The planned back end follows a layered structure: routes define the URL endpoints; middleware verifies the JSON Web Token, checks the user's role against the same permission rules used in the frontend, and validates the request body; controllers coordinate the request; and repositories execute parameterized SQL statements. Every permission that is currently enforced in the browser will be enforced again on the server, because hiding a button in the interface is a usability measure, not a security control.)
