/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 405 0 R
/T (The architecture follows a layered approach. Users in eight roles access the portal from a web browser. The React single-page application handles routing, permission checks, layout, pages, and shared components. Pages read and change data only through a shared React Context, which in turn calls the service layer. In the current release, the service layer works against an in-memory store seeded from realistic sample data; in the next phase, the same functions will send HTTP requests to an Express REST API, which will apply authentication and authorization and run SQL queries against the MySQL society_management database.)
/E (The architecture follows a layered approach. Users in eight roles access the portal from a web browser. The React single-page application handles routing, permission checks, layout, pages, and shared components. Pages read and change data only through a shared React Context, which in turn calls the service layer. In the current release, the service layer works against an in-memory store seeded from realistic sample data; in the next phase, the same functions will send HTTP requests to an Express REST API, which will apply authentication and authorization and run SQL queries against the MySQL society_management database.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
