/T (The service layer separates the user interface from the data source. api.js exposes asynchronous CRUD functions and generates convenient named helpers for each resource. auth.js handles sign- in, sign-out, and reading the current user. Because every function returns a Promise, the pages already handle data asynchronously, exactly as they will when real network calls are introduced.)
