/T (Version control and continuous integration. Source code is pushed to a GitHub repository. A continuous-integration workflow \(for example GitHub Actions\) can run on every push and pull request with three steps: npm ci to install the exact locked dependency versions, npm run lint to check code quality, and npm run build to confirm that the production bundle compiles. A pull request is merged only when these checks pass.)
/E (Version control and continuous integration. Source code is pushed to a GitHub repository. A continuous-integration workflow \(for example GitHub Actions\) can run on every push and pull request with three steps: npm ci to install the exact locked dependency versions, npm run lint to check code quality, and npm run build to confirm that the production bundle compiles. A pull request is merged only when these checks pass.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1017 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 408 0 R
/T (Frontend hosting. The output of npm run build is a static dist/ folder containing index.html, one hashed JavaScript file, and one hashed CSS file. This folder can be served by any static host or content delivery network. Vercel and Netlify are the recommended platforms because they connect directly to the GitHub repository, build automatically on every push to main, provide free HTTPS certificates, and create preview deployments for pull requests. Because the application uses client- side routing, the host is configured to rewrite all paths to index.html, so that refreshing a page such as /payments does not return a 404 error.)
/E (Frontend hosting. The output of npm run build is a static dist/ folder containing index.html, one hashed JavaScript file, and one hashed CSS file. This folder can be served by any static host or content delivery network. Vercel and Netlify are the recommended platforms because they connect directly to the GitHub repository, build automatically on every push to main, provide free HTTPS certificates, and create preview deployments for pull requests. Because the application uses client- side routing, the host is configured to rewrite all paths to index.html, so that refreshing a page such as /payments does not return a 404 error.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1018 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 408 0 R
/T (Backend and database hosting \(planned\). The Express API will be deployed to a Node.js hosting service such as Render, Railway, or an AWS EC2 instance, and the MySQL database to a managed service such as AWS RDS, Railway MySQL, or Aiven. The frontend will read the API base URL from an environment variable \(VITE_API_URL\), and secrets such as the database password and JWT signing key will be stored as environment variables on the server, never in the repository.)
/E (Backend and database hosting \(planned\). The Express API will be deployed to a Node.js hosting service such as Render, Railway, or an AWS EC2 instance, and the MySQL database to a managed service such as AWS RDS, Railway MySQL, or Aiven. The frontend will read the API base URL from an environment variable \(VITE_API_URL\), and secrets such as the database password and JWT signing key will be stored as environment variables on the server, never in the repository.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
