/T (The diagram shows ten entities. FLATS is the central property entity: one flat can have many residents, many visitors, and many maintenance bills. RESIDENTS is the central people entity: one resident can make many payments, raise many complaints, and make many amenity bookings. Each PAYMENT belongs to exactly one maintenance bill and one resident, and each AMENITY_BOOKING links one resident to one amenity. STAFF and NOTICES are independent entities that do not reference other tables.)
