<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 433 0 R
/T (Frontend hosting. The frontend is hosted as static files on a CDN-backed platform. Static hosting is ideal for this application because the server only has to deliver three files; all rendering happens in the user's browser. Vercel and Netlify both offer a free tier that comfortably covers a society portal, automatic HTTPS certificates, global edge caching, and Git-based deployments. Hashed filenames \(for example index-BG1OJBxa.js\) allow the CDN to cache assets for a long time while guaranteeing that users receive the new version after each deployment.)
/E (Frontend hosting. The frontend is hosted as static files on a CDN-backed platform. Static hosting is ideal for this application because the server only has to deliver three files; all rendering happens in the user's browser. Vercel and Netlify both offer a free tier that comfortably covers a society portal, automatic HTTPS certificates, global edge caching, and Git-based deployments. Hashed filenames \(for example index-BG1OJBxa.js\) allow the CDN to cache assets for a long time while guaranteeing that users receive the new version after each deployment.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1954 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 433 0 R
/T (Backend hosting \(planned\). The Express API will run on a platform-as-a-service such as Render or Railway, which builds the Node.js application from GitHub and restarts it automatically if it stops. For larger societies, an AWS EC2 instance with PM2 as the process manager and Nginx as a reverse proxy is an alternative.)
/E (Backend hosting \(planned\). The Express API will run on a platform-as-a-service such as Render or Railway, which builds the Node.js application from GitHub and restarts it automatically if it stops. For larger societies, an AWS EC2 instance with PM2 as the process manager and Nginx as a reverse proxy is an alternative.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
