/Title (A key design decision was to describe each module declaratively in src/config/resources.js. For every resource, the configuration lists the page title, the primary-key field, the table columns and how each should be displayed \(plain text, status badge, currency, date, or a relationship such as flat or resident\), the form fields with their types and validation rules, the filter fields, and the summary statistics. The generic ResourcePage reads this configuration and produces a complete page with statistics cards, a search box, filters, a sortable and paginated table, and add, edit, view, and delete dialogs. As a result, the Flats, Residents, Visitors, Staff, Maintenance, Payments, Complaints, and Bookings pages each require only a two-line page file.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 9442 0 R
>>
endobj
