/Title (MySQL 8 was chosen as the database because society data is naturally relational. Flats have residents; flats receive bills; bills receive payments made by residents; residents raise complaints and book amenities. These relationships are best represented with tables, primary keys, and foreign keys, and they benefit from the integrity guarantees of a relational database management system.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 9465 0 R
/Next 9475 0 R
>>
endobj
9470 0 obj
<<
/Title (The sample data in src/data/mockData.js mirrors the exact column names and foreign-key relationships of the MySQL tables: 12 flats across three blocks, 10 residents, 8 visitors, 6 staff members, 11 maintenance bills, 8 payments, 6 complaints, 5 notices, 5 amenities, and 8 amenity bookings. Because the frontend already uses the database column names, connecting to the real database will not require changes to the table or form configuration.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
