/Title (Postman is used to test HTTP APIs by sending requests and checking the status code and response body. Because the current release uses an in-memory service layer instead of a running server, the Postman work in this phase focused on defining and documenting the REST contract that the backend must satisfy, so that the backend can be verified immediately once it is built. The contract was derived directly from the service functions \(list, add, update, remove\) and the column names used by the frontend.)
